<title>BELGIUM: Belgian FX reserves down on EMI swap renewal.</title>
<headline>Belgian FX reserves down on EMI swap renewal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said in its weekly statement on Wednesday that its foreign exchange reserves fell and Ecu reserves rose in the week to April 14 following the quarterly renewal of swap credits between the bank and the European Monetary Institue.</p>
<p>The changes are due to the rise of the dollar and gold prices in the past quarter.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   441.78 (-  8.74)</p>
<p> Ecus					 93.83 (+ 10.82)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  16.28 (+  3.12)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.49 (-  0.17)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.81 (unchanged)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 101.85 (+  1.21)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   459.36 (-  0.63)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
